BLOSUM is a symmetric 20 × 20 matrix constructed by Henikoff et al., in46, where each entry is proportional to the probability of substitution of a given amino acids with another amino acid in a protein (substitution probability in evolutionarily related proteins). Each entry in this matrix can be represented using the following equation:1\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
				\usepackage{amsmath}
